  <p>
    I'm Christopher — a country and economic research analyst specializing in Vietnam and Southeast
    Asia. I spent four years living and building a consultancy in Hà Nội, developing on-the-ground
    knowledge of Vietnam's regulatory environment, business landscape, and policy dynamics. I speak,
    read, and write Vietnamese at an advanced level, with working Bahasa Indonesia and elementary
    Thai. My graduate training combines an MA in Southeast Asian Studies
    (<a href="https://www.soas.ac.uk/">SOAS, University of London</a>, Distinction) with an MSc in
    Development Economics (<a href="http://www.city.ac.uk">City, University of London</a>,
    Distinction), giving me both the area-studies depth and the quantitative toolkit to produce
    policy- and investment-relevant analysis of the region.
  </p>

